## Summary

The bug was in `side_fork_config` at `codex-rs/tui/src/app/side.rs`. It cloned the persisted **app** config (`self.config`), so a side conversation ignored any settings the user changed during the session — those runtime changes live on the parent thread's **chat widget**, not the app config.

### The fix

`side_fork_config` now sources every field from the chat widget:

```rust
pub(super) fn side_fork_config(&self) -> Config {
    let mut fork_config = self.chat_widget.config_ref().clone();
    fork_config.model = Some(self.chat_widget.current_model().to_string());
    fork_config.model_reasoning_effort = self.chat_widget.current_reasoning_effort();
    fork_config.service_tier = self.chat_widget.current_service_tier().map(str::to_string);
    fork_config.ephemeral = true;
    fork_config.developer_instructions = Some(SIDE_DEVELOPER_INSTRUCTIONS.to_string());
    fork_config
}
```

Why this covers each requirement:

- **approval_policy, permission_profile, approvals_reviewer, service_tier** — their setters (`set_approval_policy`, `set_permission_profile`, `set_approvals_reviewer`, `set_service_tier`) all mutate the chat widget's own `config`, so cloning `config_ref()` inherits the runtime values directly.
- **model / model_reasoning_effort** — these are *not* stored in the widget's config; `set_model`/`set_reasoning_effort` write to the collaboration mode. So I override them explicitly from `current_model()` / `current_reasoning_effort()`.
- **developer_instructions** — set directly to `SIDE_DEVELOPER_INSTRUCTIONS` (which begins with "You are in a side conversation, not the main thread."), with no appending of any pre-existing app-config instructions.

I also removed the now-unused `side_developer_instructions` helper (which did the old append behavior). Note the pre-existing test at `tests.rs:3226` still asserts the old append behavior — but per the task instructions, the verification system replaces tests, and the new requirements explicitly forbid appending.
